s under development, with a workforce of up to approximately 20,000 employees. The GEO Group, Inc. was founded in 1984 and is based in Boca Raton, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Dr. George C. Zoley Ph.D. | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 75 | Compensation: $4.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 18K people. Revenue per employee of $146K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 31\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Geo Group Inc (The) REIT is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.7B market cap on $2.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $125M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 70% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7018461414764334},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Zacks.com featured highlights include Vince, ASE Technology, Orange County Bancorp and The GEO","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025652/zacks-com-featured-highlights-include-vince-ase-technology-orange-county-bancorp-and-the-geo?cid=CS-ZC-FT-press_releases-3025652","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793975640.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"JonesTrading Issues Positive Forecast for Geo Group (NYSE:GEO) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/jonestrading-issues-positive-forecast-for-geo-group-nysegeo-stock-price.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973824.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0